Hello everyone!


Today's patch tries to ease and make the game more comfortable for people sensitive to light.



The Glitch Effect in particular can cause a lot of discomfort for some players. If you are sensible in any way to lights or bright patterns we highly suggest it to be disabled.



SETTINGS

All the following settings were added to the Graphics Section

Added a Bloom Slider;

Added a Film Grain Slider;

Added a Glitch Effect Slider;



BUG FIXES

Fixed a mistranslation for Research Scrap B in Brazilian Portuguese;

Fixed the rotation of the Scraps being inverted;



If you experience any bugs and would like to report, feel free to share them with us on our official discord!  



Have a great day, 

and be wary of the dark.

Hi everyone! 



First and foremost, we really want to thank you for playing the game and would like to apologize for any inconveniences caused by bugs on the release day.



Players that previously played the Blasfemia Demo may have their save files corrupted.
What does a corrupted save file compromises?
[olist]
Earn a selection of achievements;

Find Collectibles;
[/olist]


Because of this I implemented in haste some features:


SAVE DATA MANAGEMENT

A new option named "Save Data" was put in the "Settings" that allow Players to reset their progress (New Game+, Specialist Mode and Collectibles) or only Collectibles;



SAVE DATA CORRUPTION DETECTION

If your save files was compromised by the Demo a Warning will pop up in the main menu notifying you about it and asking if you want to proceed with corrections or ignore them;

Once again, we're truly sorry for the inconveniences this could have caused.



GAME VERSION WATERMARK

We removed the game version being visible at all times due to Player feedback. It will only show in the Main Menu now.



JAPANESE LOCALIZATION

Unfortunately, we could not get the Japanese Localization ready for release date but we're working hard to ship it in a future update as fast as we can. We're sorry for this!  



BUG FIXES

Fixed a Bug with Clara's Research Diary on Act III that caused Fire, Water and Wind translations not work at all;

Fixed a Bug with Ranking Calculation that would set Ranks outside of S, A, B and C;

Fixed a Bug with skipping the First Tape that could lead to a soft lock;



KNOW ISSUES

The Nun during Act III may cause a lingering "Glitch Effect" on Player's screen if spotted from within the Bathroom;

Not all Collectibles will show up on the Gallery as soon as they're picked up;

Inventory Items will not localize correctly if the game language is changed during gameplay;


If you experienced bugs and want to report them, feel free to join us on discord and share it with us!  


Have a great day, 

and be wary of the dark.
